xnu 0190: hold the GMU keepalive from cp_start, not from the first submission

CoreAnimation's first frame reaches the user client minutes after the CP was
started. The keepalive is only raised inside a submission, so the GMU has the
GPU parked when that frame arrives, and the rings show the CP never fetching
those packets: CP_RB_RPTR stays equal to CP_RB_WPTR right after a submission
that the CPU then dies in. gpukeep=1 now raises the keepalive once, right after
the SQE is started, and never drops it.

HackiOS reaches the same place with explicit pauses in its GPU bring-up
(`adreno_pause`), which is what pointed at the parked GPU rather than at the
stream.

--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_gpu.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_gpu.c
@@ -2429,6 +2429,18 @@
 
 	printf("MONDRIAN GPU: cp started\n");
 	mondrian_log_flush_now();
+	/*
+	 * CoreAnimation's first frame arrives minutes after this, and the
+	 * GMU parks the GPU while it waits. The keepalive is otherwise only
+	 * raised inside a submission, so the first frame is rung into a parked
+	 * GPU and the CP never fetches it (CP_RB_RPTR stays at CP_RB_WPTR).
+	 * gpukeep=1 keeps it up from here on.
+	 */
+	if (mondrian_uc_gmu != 0 && mondrian_uc_keep == 1) {
+		mondrian_gpu_write(mondrian_uc_gmu, GMU_OFF(0x1f8c3u), 1);
+		printf("MONDRIAN GPU: cp keepalive held up\n");
+		mondrian_log_flush_now();
+	}
 
 	for (i = 0; i < 2000; i++) {
 		rptr = CPR(GEN7_CP_RB_RPTR);
